WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.360
Arc is also how many organizations keep

2
00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:05.300
end-of-support servers
patched while they migrate.

3
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:11.519
As of October twentieth, 2026: the
Windows Server 2012 and 2012 R2 ESU period

4
00:00:11.519 --> 00:00:17.738
ended on October thirteenth, and Arc
ESU licenses deactivated the next day.

5
00:00:17.738 --> 00:00:20.058
Any such host still running receives no

6
00:00:20.058 --> 00:00:22.800
further security updates
through any channel.

7
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.823
Treat it as a red finding:
migrate, upgrade,

8
00:00:25.823 --> 00:00:29.112
or isolate it and record
the risk acceptance.

9
00:00:29.112 --> 00:00:34.165
Windows Server 2016 reaches end of
support on January twelfth, 2027,

10
00:00:34.165 --> 00:00:37.863
with ESUs for up to three
years; connect and enroll

11
00:00:37.863 --> 00:00:42.013
those hosts before then if they
won't be upgraded in time.

12
00:00:42.013 --> 00:00:47.959
SQL Server 2014 is in its third
ESU year, until July 2027,

13
00:00:47.959 --> 00:00:53.113
and SQL Server 2016 in its
first, until July 2029.

14
00:00:53.113 --> 00:00:55.494
ESUs through Arc are billed monthly,

15
00:00:55.494 --> 00:00:58.750
need no product keys, and
show coverage per server.

16
00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:00.512
Entra ID sign-in.

17
00:01:00.512 --> 00:01:05.034
Arc-enabled Windows servers can
use Entra ID for Remote Desktop,

18
00:01:05.034 --> 00:01:07.763
with Azure RBAC deciding who signs in.

19
00:01:07.763 --> 00:01:14.875
It needs Windows Server 2025 or later with
Desktop Experience, or Windows 11 24H2;

20
00:01:14.875 --> 00:01:20.501
2019 and 2022 aren't supported,
which is exception C from Module 1.

21
00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:23.775
It's available in Azure
Global and Azure Government.

22
00:01:23.775 --> 00:01:27.237
Installing the sign-in extension
Entra-joins the server,

23
00:01:27.237 --> 00:01:29.963
so it's for servers that
won't be domain-joined.

24
00:01:29.963 --> 00:01:33.151
Only member users of the
same tenant can sign in.

25
00:01:33.151 --> 00:01:37.887
And Conditional Access isn't supported
with the join extension on Arc servers.

26
00:01:37.887 --> 00:01:42.846
That corrects a common assumption: the
control you get is RBAC on who may sign in,

27
00:01:42.846 --> 00:01:46.226
held through PIM, not
workstation Conditional Access.

28
00:01:46.226 --> 00:01:50.900
Linux uses SSH through Arc with its
own extension and the same roles.

29
00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:54.054
Rollback order matters:
remove extensions first,

30
00:01:54.054 --> 00:01:58.439
because uninstalling the agent
leaves them behind; then disconnect,

31
00:01:58.439 --> 00:02:02.420
which needs the resource
administrator role; then uninstall.
